  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466486",
      "title": "What are Modules?",
      "lectureOrder": 646,
      "videoOrder": 594,
      "sourceHash": "1f8f924f9b779f3cde00ece491e89e810c9e318618e74c482919c3529a86f481",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.837,
          "end": 4.41,
          "en": "Instructor: What are modules?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.41,
          "end": 7.47,
          "en": "And with that, I mean the angular modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.47,
          "end": 10.147,
          "en": "You will also hear the term module when you are talking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.147,
          "end": 12.84,
          "en": "about the imports you have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.84,
          "end": 15.63,
          "en": "in your files when you import something from another file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.63,
          "end": 18.57,
          "en": "into another file, that also is sometimes referred",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.57,
          "end": 21.81,
          "en": "to as modules, but these would be JavaScript modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.81,
          "end": 23.7,
          "en": "They're totally not related to Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.7,
          "end": 24.96,
          "en": "they're not what I mean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.96,
          "end": 28.83,
          "en": "I mean that NG module thing that we have in our app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.83,
          "end": 31.987,
          "en": "like the app module or the app routing module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.987,
          "end": 34.255,
          "en": "So modules in the end are ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.255,
          "end": 37.89,
          "en": "of bundling Angular building blocks together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.89,
          "end": 41.777,
          "en": "That would be components, directives, services, pipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.777,
          "end": 44.52,
          "en": "You have to group that all together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.52,
          "end": 47.22,
          "en": "into such Angular modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.22,
          "end": 50.13,
          "en": "so that Angular is aware of these features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.13,
          "end": 53.238,
          "en": "because Angular doesn't automatically scan all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.238,
          "end": 55.32,
          "en": "the files in your project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.32,
          "end": 57.6,
          "en": "It doesn't search all the code you write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.6,
          "end": 60.619,
          "en": "and automatically detect all components and services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.619,
          "end": 64.44,
          "en": "Instead, you need to tell Angular what is a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.44,
          "end": 66.09,
          "en": "which components do you have?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.09,
          "end": 69.286,
          "en": "And you can then bundle them together into modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.286,
          "end": 71.88,
          "en": "Every Angular app needs to have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.88,
          "end": 74.94,
          "en": "at least one module, that app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.94,
          "end": 77.31,
          "en": "You can't have an Angular app without it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.31,
          "end": 79.95,
          "en": "So Angular analyzes these engine modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.95,
          "end": 83.1,
          "en": "to understand your application and its features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.1,
          "end": 86.31,
          "en": "You use them to define all the core building blocks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.31,
          "end": 90.03,
          "en": "components, directives, services, pipes, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.03,
          "end": 91.5,
          "en": "An app, as I just mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.5,
          "end": 94.136,
          "en": "requires at least one such module, the app module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.136,
          "end": 97.17,
          "en": "but you may split it into multiple modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.17,
          "end": 100.21600000000001,
          "en": "and we will do that in this course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 100.21600000000001,
          "end": 103.11,
          "en": "You also have core Angular features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 103.11,
          "end": 106.08,
          "en": "that are wrapped into modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 106.08,
          "end": 107.72999999999999,
          "en": "Things like the forms module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.72999999999999,
          "end": 109.65,
          "en": "which we added in the course already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 109.65,
          "end": 113.28,
          "en": "So Angular itself also provides certain features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 113.28,
          "end": 115.74000000000001,
          "en": "grouped to gather into such modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 115.74000000000001,
          "end": 117.75800000000001,
          "en": "so that you don't have to declare",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 117.75800000000001,
          "end": 120.96,
          "en": "like 10 different forms directives instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 120.96,
          "end": 123.36,
          "en": "that forms module gives you all these directives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 123.36,
          "end": 125.4,
          "en": "That is how you can think about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 125.4,
          "end": 128.632,
          "en": "And important also, you can't use a certain feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 128.632,
          "end": 132.45,
          "en": "or building block without including it in a module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 132.45,
          "end": 135.45,
          "en": "How you include it, if you add it to declarations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 135.45,
          "end": 139.781,
          "en": "or providers, depends on the feature you are talking about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 139.781,
          "end": 141.45,
          "en": "So let's have a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 141.45,
          "end": 144.183,
          "en": "at our app module and what we're using thus far.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
